	<key>readme</key>
	<string># Sync Pad

Share clipboard text with your other Macs. This is separate from Alfred Clipboard History.

Type `pad` in Alfred. The newest Sync Pad snippets are listed first. Clipboard history follows them.

- Return copies the highlighted clip and makes it the newest clipboard item.
- Command-Return saves that clip to Sync Pad. The pad keeps the last 30 clips. Sharing the same text again moves it to the top.
- Option-Return removes a shared clip.

Shared clips are stored in `sync-pad.json` next to your synced Alfred preferences folder, so Google Drive carries them to the other Macs. Give Drive a moment before looking on the other computer.

Open `pad` on the other Mac and press Return on the shared clip. Alfred puts it on the clipboard and into Clipboard History.

The pad is plain text. Share only what you would put in Google Drive.
</string>
